{title: 039 - Lord, in the Morning}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #039 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 39}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Lord, in [C]the [F]morn[Dm]ing Thou [F]shalt [C]hear
[C]My [F]voice as[C]cend[G]ing [C]high;
[F]To [Bb]Thee [C]will [F]I [Dm]di[Bb]rect [F]my [C]prayer,
[Dm]To [C]Thee [F]lift [Bb]up [C7]mine [F]eye—
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Up [C]to [F]the hills [Dm]where [F]Christ [C]is gone
[C]To [F]plead [C]for [G]all [C]His saints,
[F][Bb]Presenting [C][F]at [Dm]His [Bb][F]Father's [C]throne
[Dm][C]Our [F]songs [Bb]and [C7]our [F]complaints.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]O [C]may [F]Thy [Dm]Spirit [F]guide [C]my feet
[C][F]In [C]ways [G]of [C]righteousness;
[F][Bb]Make [C]every [F]path [Dm][Bb]of [F]duty [C]straight
[Dm][C]And [F]plain [Bb]before [C7]my [F]face.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]The [C]men [F]that love [Dm]and [F]fear [C]Thy name
[C]Shall [F]see [C]their [G]hopes [C]fulfilled;
[F][Bb]The [C]mighty [F]God [Dm][Bb]will [F]compass [C]them
[Dm][C]With [F]favor [Bb]as [C7]a [F]shield.
{end_of_verse}
